      "writtenOn": "2021-08-31T11:00:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IIUC, this will wrap after 255 (it\u0027s an array of u8) and the nonce won\u0027t be unique any more so it should error when that happens. Or make the nonce _be_ the count and error when that overflows. (Do we need more than once nonce for this application, could it just fail after the first call like [1]? Or even use the LessSafeKey API talked about in [2].)\n\n[1] -- https://github.com/briansmith/ring/blob/20582aa39a0d57ff1dac5522cbeae4abcd039bd9/tests/aead_tests.rs#L439\n[2] -- https://github.com/briansmith/ring/issues/899",
